{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>After HaShem your Elohim you shall walk</b>. This is a commandment that we walk after His counsel, and from Him alone do we seek out every hidden thing and inquire about everything future, in the manner of \"and she went to inquire of HaShem\" (Genesis 25:22), \"the people come to me to inquire of Elohim\" (Exodus 18:15). And so Israel would do with the prophets: \"Is there not here a prophet of HaShem, that we may inquire of HaShem by him?\" (II Kings 3:11), \"and HaShem your Elohim tell us the way wherein we should walk, and the thing that we should do\" (Jeremiah 42:3). And in the Sifre: \"After HaShem your Elohim\" — this refers to the cloud. And this is what we explained, that we obey the voice of His signs and walk after His counsel:" "<b>and Him you shall fear</b> — that you believe that He it is in whose hand is the soul of every living thing, and in whose hand it is to kill and to bring to life, visiting iniquity and rendering reward:" "<b>and His commandments you shall keep</b> — the Torah of Moses:" "<b>and His voice you shall obey</b> — to do everything He commands us apart from the Torah, as Samuel said (I Samuel 13:13), \"You have acted foolishly; you have not kept the commandment of HaShem.\" And this is what He further explains (Deuteronomy 18:15): \"A prophet from your midst, from your brothers, like me, HaShem your Elohim will raise up for you — to him you shall listen,\" and He said (ibid. v. 19), \"And the man who does not listen — I Myself will require it from him,\" meaning that he is liable to death by the hand of Heaven, as is related in the commandment of the prophet: \"Be struck, and wound me, by the word of HaShem\" (I Kings 20:35–37). And so they said in the Sifre (Re'eh 60): \"and His voice you shall obey\" — in the voice of His prophets:" "<b>and Him you shall serve and to Him you shall cling</b>. I have already explained this (above, 6:13, 11, 22). Now, it has already been stated (Deuteronomy 6:13), \"HaShem your Elohim you shall fear, and Him you shall serve,\" but He repeated it here to negate the possibility that we might fear the words of the prophet on account of the sign and the portent, and that we might transgress the service of HaShem because of his words — for from HaShem alone do we fear, and not from any other el — and to add, \"and His voice you shall obey\":"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The word עָנָן ('cloud') in the Sifre citation refers to the pillar of cloud that guided Israel in the wilderness.", 3 "The Sifre citation is given as 'ראה ס' which appears to be a section number; I have rendered it as Re'eh 60 following the standard numbering convention.", 4 "The phrase 'החזירו בכאן' (literally 'He repeated/returned it here') is rendered as 'He repeated it here'; some witnesses may read differently but the sense is stable."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:49:40.831469644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}